    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d524">

                <pb facs="0520" n="508" xml:id="pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.24591/14</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Iranian Legation to the Department of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1309</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department of State is aware of the frequent complaints which have been
                    received about the conduct of some of the American soldiers in Iran. In
                    particular, their behaviour towards women has excited public comment and has
                    been deplored by the Press.</p>
                <p>More incidents have lately been reported and recently an Iranian chauffeur was
                    killed and another severely wounded by American soldiers at Arak.</p>
                <p>The Iranian Government is most anxious that nothing should happen to impair the
                    high esteem and good opinion which the Iranians have always held towards the
                    American people. It has, therefore, instructed this Legation to bring the matter
                    to the notice of the United States Government in order that the War Department
                    might take the necessary steps to avoid a repetition of such incidents.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1943-09-20">September 20,
                            1943</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
